BT /F2 13 Tf 44.0 500.0 Td (Tiny Meaning) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 44.0 480.0 Td (The backend is the hidden kitchen of the HR app. The frontend is what users see. The backend stores data, reads) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 44.0 466.0 Td (resumes, checks job descriptions, matches candidates, schedules interviews, and talks to AI.) Tj ET
BT /F2 13 Tf 44.0 442.0 Td (Main Idea) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 54.0 422.0 Td (- routes are the doors where frontend requests enter.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 54.0 407.0 Td (- services are the workers that do business logic.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 54.0 392.0 Td (- database.py is the big notebook that remembers jobs, candidates, interviews, users, and audit logs.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 54.0 377.0 Td (- agents are AI helpers for reading, matching, ranking, summarizing, and chatting.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 54.0 362.0 Td (- LangGraph is the traffic controller that decides which agent runs first and next.) Tj ET
BT /F2 13 Tf 44.0 339.0 Td (Like You Are 5) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 44.0 319.0 Td (Imagine an office helper. One helper opens the door, one writes in the notebook, one reads papers, one compares) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 44.0 305.0 Td (papers, one makes a list of best people, and one explains the answer. LangGraph tells these helpers whose turn it is.) Tj ET
q 0.7 w 44.0 34.0 m 798.0 34.0 l S Q
BT /F1 7 Tf 44.0 19.0 Td (RecruitmentAssist - Backend and LangGraph Explanation) Tj ET
