BT /F2 13 Tf 44.0 500.0 Td (Where It Lives) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 44.0 480.0 Td (LangGraph is mainly used in RecruitmentAssist/backend/orchestration/hr_graph.py.) Tj ET
BT /F2 13 Tf 44.0 458.0 Td (What It Does) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 54.0 438.0 Td (- It creates a StateGraph named HRGraphState.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 54.0 423.0 Td (- It adds nodes such as router, jd_agent, resume_agent, matching_agent, ranking_agent, summary_agent,) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 54.0 410.0 Td (recruiter_chat_agent, and final_response.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 54.0 395.0 Td (- It connects nodes with edges, which means after this step, go to that step.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 54.0 380.0 Td (- It uses conditional edges after the router so only the correct path runs.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 54.0 365.0 Td (- It returns one final response shape back to Flask and then the frontend.) Tj ET
BT /F2 13 Tf 44.0 342.0 Td (The Shared Backpack) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 44.0 322.0 Td (HRGraphState is like a backpack passed from node to node. It can carry payload, username, run_id, task_type, route) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 44.0 308.0 Td (decision, jd_id, JD context, resume context, match result, ranking result, summary, errors, and final_response.) Tj ET
